outputs.exact_statement:
There is a deterministic sequence $a_n=a_n(q)>0$ with $a_n\to0$ such that, through all positive integers, $$\label{intro:joint-convergence}
 \big((\phi_n)_*m_n,K_n(a_n),\Gamma_n\big)
 \ \Longrightarrow\
 \big(\mu_h,\{(z,w,D_h(z,w)):z,w\in\widehat{\mathbb C}\},\Gamma\big).$$ The three topologies are weak convergence of probability measures, Hausdorff convergence of the full distance graphs, and uniform reparameterization matching of loop collections as defined in <a href="#intro:loop-topology" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="intro:loop-topology">5</a>. Moreover, $$\label{intro:mesh-conclusion}
 \max_{T\text{ a flag triangle of }X_n}
       \mathop{\mathrm{diam}}_{\rho}\phi_n(T)\ \longrightarrow\ 0
 \qquad\text{in probability},$$ where $\rho$ is spherical distance. The conditional law of $\Gamma$ is independent of the embedded marked quantum surface.

There are sphere homeomorphisms $H_n:X_n\to S$ such that $$\label{top:homeomorphism-error}
 \sup_{x\in X_n}\rho(H_n(x),P_n(x))\longrightarrow0.$$ In particular, $$\label{top:homeomorphism-mesh}
 \max_{T}\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}_\rho H_n(T)\longrightarrow0,$$ and the images under $H_n$ of every flag and all its tour representatives have vanishing maximum disagreement. The maps may preserve or reverse orientation, with a common sign on each sphere. They may be chosen measurably in the contour coupling. The assertion continues to hold when that coupling retains any additional random observations.

Set $$\theta=\arccos(-\varrho)=\frac{\pi\gamma^2}{4},\qquad
 d_0=0,\quad d_1=\frac12,\quad d_2=\frac{\pi}{2\theta}
       =\frac2{\gamma^2}>\frac12.$$ For fixed positive duration, the probability that Brownian motion stays above $-\varepsilon$ in $k$ specified coordinates is at most $C\varepsilon^{2d_k}$, for $k=1,2$. Constants may depend on a compact range of positive durations. A fixed-start killed transition probability ending with those $k$ coordinates in an $\varepsilon$-neighborhood of the walls is at most $C\varepsilon^{k+2d_k}$, with start points in a compact set. Finally, on a compact time window and for fixed positive record witness, the image in $\mathbb R^2$ of the joint record times has upper box dimension at most $$\label{enc:record-image-dimension}
 2(1-d_2)<1.$$ The same bound holds for either coordinate projection of this image.

Let $c$ be one of the two limiting contours on a compact interval $J$. Let $I\subset J$ be open and contain $\eta^{-1}(K)\cap J$ for a compact set $K$, and let $O=J\setminus I$. Consider a compact family $\mathcal C$ of triples $(s,t,h)$, $s\le t$, such that $$c(s)=c(t)=h,\qquad \eta(s)\in K,\qquad
 c(u)\ge h\quad (u\in[s,t]\cap I).$$ There is $\delta>0$ such that, whenever $[s,t]\cap O\ne\varnothing$ and $(s,t,h)\in\mathcal C$, $$\label{top:minimum-gap}
 \left|\min_{[s,t]\cap O}c-h\right|>\delta.$$ Consequently the omitted pieces cannot change an exact gluing decision at heights tending to a protected candidate height without either a retained obstruction or a strict height gap.

Let $I,O,A$ be Polish variables, with $O$ compact: retained intrinsic input, output, and additional input, respectively. Let $\widehat e_n$ be a frozen microscopic exterior with macroscopic record $e_n$. On a fixed good chart suppose that along every sequence $e_n\to e$, $$R_n^{\widehat e_n}\Longrightarrow R_e(\mathrm dI,\mathrm dA)K(I,\mathrm dO).
 \label{ker:reference-limit}$$ Suppose the actual conditional resampling law is exactly $$Q_n^{\widehat e_n}
 =\frac{W_n^{\widehat e_n}}{R_n^{\widehat e_n}[W_n^{\widehat e_n}]}
 R_n^{\widehat e_n}.
 \label{ker:exact-ratio}$$ Factors depending only on $n,\widehat e_n$ may be canceled. If the weights are bounded on this chart and converge jointly to $w(e,I,A)$, with positive limiting normalizer, the limiting conditional output kernel remains $K$. This holds for finite products of independent complete reference packages, and after integration of auxiliary variables absent from the finite readout.

Let $g$ be the density of $(\tau_1^\circ,R^\circ_{\tau_1^\circ})$. It is bounded and positive smooth for $t>0$, and $$\sup_{\substack{k\ge1,\ \ell\in\mathbb Z\\k-m-\ell\in2\mathbb Z}}
 \left|m^3p_m(k,\ell)-2g(k/m^2,\ell/m)\right|\longrightarrow0.
 \label{ker:llt}$$ The probabilities vanish off that parity coset. For admissible endpoint sequences converging in these units to $(t,y)$, $t>0$, the entire stopped contour converges conditionally to the Brownian first-passage bridge with that endpoint and duration. The convergence is uniform on compact interior sets of scaled depth, duration, and second displacement. Strictly admissible open uniform path tubes have positive limiting probability.

